# 📦 PART 1: The Foundational 50%

---

### Module 1: Core Fundamentals & Virtual DOM
- [ ] What is React? (Library vs Framework, SPA vs MPA)
- [ ] React DOM vs React Core
- [ ] The Virtual DOM (VDOM) mental model
- [ ] Reconciliation & Diffing Algorithm overview
- [ ] React root mounting (`createRoot` from `react-dom/client`)
- [ ] `StrictMode` and why it renders twice in development

### Module 2: JSX (JavaScript XML) In-Depth
- [ ] JSX compilation under the hood (`React.createElement` / JSX transform)
- [ ] JSX Syntax rules (Single root, self-closing tags, camelCase attributes)
- [ ] HTML vs JSX attribute differences (`className`, `htmlFor`, `tabIndex`, `style` object)
- [ ] Embedding JavaScript expressions with curly braces `{}`
- [ ] React Fragments (`<React.Fragment>` vs `<> ... </>`)
- [ ] Rendering strings, numbers, booleans, null, and undefined in JSX
- [ ] White space handling & HTML entity decoding in JSX

### Module 3: Component Architecture
- [ ] Functional Components vs Legacy Class Components
- [ ] Pure Functions & Component Purity rules
- [ ] Component Composition (building UI trees)
- [ ] File organization & folder structuring conventions
- [ ] Exporting and importing components (Default vs Named exports)

### Module 4: Props & One-Way Data Flow
- [ ] Passing props from Parent to Child
- [ ] Props Destructuring (standard, nested, and default prop values)
- [ ] The special `children` prop (Containment & Slots pattern)
- [ ] Prop Types & Type Safety (`PropTypes` / TypeScript interfaces)
- [ ] Props immutability (Why props are read-only)
- [ ] Passing functions as props (Callback props)

### Module 5: Conditional Rendering
- [ ] `if / else` statements outside JSX
- [ ] Ternary operator (`condition ? <A /> : <B />`)
- [ ] Logical AND operator (`condition && <Element />`)
- [ ] The falsy `0` bug in logical AND and how to prevent it
- [ ] Early returns (`if (!data) return null;`)
- [ ] Switch-case statements & Object mapping patterns for multi-state UI

### Module 6: Rendering Lists & Keys
- [ ] Transforming arrays using JavaScript `.map()`
- [ ] Filtering before rendering (`.filter().map()`)
- [ ] The `key` prop: What it is and why React requires it
- [ ] How React uses keys for VDOM identity & element recycling
- [ ] Pitfalls of using array `index` as a key
- [ ] Rendering nested arrays and multi-dimensional lists

### Module 7: Event Handling & Synthetic Events
- [ ] Adding event listeners in JSX (`onClick`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`, `onKeyDown`, etc.)
- [ ] Passing a function reference vs calling a function inline
- [ ] Passing arguments to event handlers via arrow functions
- [ ] React's Synthetic Event Wrapper (`SyntheticEvent`)
- [ ] Event methods: `e.preventDefault()` and `e.stopPropagation()`
- [ ] Event pooling (legacy) vs modern event delegation

### Module 8: Foundational Hooks — State & References
- [ ] **Rules of Hooks**: Only call at top level, only call from React functions
- [ ] **`useState` Hook**:
  - Initial state values & lazy state initialization (`useState(() => expensiveComputation())`)
  - State updater function syntax (`setState(prev => prev + 1)`)
  - State as a snapshot (Why state doesn't update immediately on the next line)
  - Batching of state updates (Automatic batching in React 18+)
- [ ] **`useRef` Hook**:
  - Storing mutable values that do **not** trigger a re-render
  - Accessing direct DOM elements (`ref={myInputRef}`)
  - Tracking previous state with refs
  - Storing timer / interval IDs (`setInterval`, `setTimeout`)

### Module 9: State Architecture & Immutability Patterns
- [ ] Immutability rules in JavaScript & React
- [ ] Updating arrays in state:
  - Adding items: `[...prev, newItem]`
  - Removing items: `prev.filter(...)`
  - Updating items: `prev.map(...)`
  - Sorting & reversing: `[...prev].sort(...)`
- [ ] Updating objects in state:
  - Shallow copies using the spread operator `{ ...prev, field: value }`
  - Updating deeply nested objects
- [ ] **Lifting State Up**: Sharing state between sibling components
- [ ] **Derived State**: Calculating values on-the-fly during render vs redundant state

### Module 10: Forms & User Input
- [ ] **Controlled Components**: Binding `value` to state + listening to `onChange`
- [ ] **Uncontrolled Components**: Reading values using `useRef` or `FormData`
- [ ] Handling multiple inputs with a single state object `[e.target.name]: e.target.value`
- [ ] Checkboxes, Radio buttons, Select dropdowns, and Textareas
- [ ] Form submission handling (`onSubmit` + `e.preventDefault()`)
- [ ] Basic client-side validation techniques

